#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""phase1_one_shot_runner.py — chip-AGNOSTIC Phase 1 (doc-extraction) orchestrator.

Reads ``<project>/input/docs/`` (PDF / DOC / DOCX / XLSX / PPTX / TXT /
MD) plus ``<project>/input/otp/`` (Verilog $readmemh / .mif / .ver image
files) and emits the canonical 13 L docs into ``<project>/generated_docs/``
plus extracted text into ``<project>/input_doc/`` plus an
``<project>/reports/extraction_coverage_report.{md,json}`` with
``overall.pct = 100.0`` (or as close as the deterministic patterns can
get; remaining gaps are surfaced as TODO entries with explicit reasons).

Why this exists:
    Phase 2/3 already had ``phase23_one_shot_runner.py`` (Wave 49). But
    Phase 1 (doc-extraction) remained 17 LLM-driven plugin skills, each requiring an
    agent to read 2-5 vendor docs + write structured JSON by hand. With
    31 raw docs × 17 skills, a single fresh-agent attempt blew through
    its context budget every time before reaching Phase 2. This is the
    ``historical context-budget bottleneck`` the runner docstring named
    but did not solve.

What this runner solves:
    Drop-in deterministic extraction for the 80-90% of L doc content
    that follows recognisable protocol-IC patterns. The remaining
    10-20% needs LLM judgement and is emitted as TODO stubs that an
    agent can fill in afterwards in a small, focused turn.

Pipeline (strictly chip-AGNOSTIC):

    1. extract_text_pipeline()   — convert every PDF / DOC / DOCX /
                                    XLSX / PPTX in input/docs/ to
                                    plain UTF-8 .txt under
                                    input_doc/.
    2. l1_datasheet_gen()        — pin table + electrical specs from
                                    datasheet PDF.
    3. l2_frs_gen()              — FRS sections + protocol overview.
    4. l3_cmd_protocol_gen()     — opcodes + CRC parameters from
                                    command-spec XLSX + protocol-rule
                                    TXT.
    5. l4_regmap_gen()           — register layout + OTP IP macro
                                    cross-reference.
    6. l5_adi_spec_gen()         — analog block discovery via the
                                    Wave-47 keyword scan.
    7. l6_control_logic_gen()    — reject rules from RX/event spec
                                    + dispatcher FSM scaffold.
    8. l7_test_debug_gen()       — test mode opcodes + engineer-mode
                                    sequences.
    9. l8_timing_waveform_gen()  — RX classifier ticks + TX bit-cell
                                    constants + frame-end gap.
   10. l9_integration_spec_gen() — module hierarchy + top-level pins
                                    + ``expected_verdict_byte_hex``
                                    derived from L3 / RX_EVENT.
   11. l10_test_cases_gen()      — Phase 2c bring-up sequences + col-D
                                    coverage matrix scaffold.
   12. l11_otp_content_gen()     — 128 / 256-byte OTP image bytes
                                    parsed from input/otp/*.{hex,mif,ver}
                                    + section labels from xlsx.
   13. l12_behavioral_gen()      — host→device sequences typed steps
                                    (one per opcode in L3).
   14. l13_lab_calibration_gen() — calibration / cosim checklist from
                                    cosim_check_list / engineer-mode.
   15. emit_extraction_evidence() — every L doc carries top-level
                                    ``extraction_evidence`` mapping
                                    each source filename → list of
                                    ``{literal, label}`` entries.
   16. emit_coverage_report()    — counts unique literals across L
                                    docs vs unique literals in
                                    extracted_docs to compute
                                    ``overall.pct``.

Output schema follows existing plugin gates exactly so downstream
``extraction_evidence_schema_check`` / ``phase1_coverage_report_present_check``
/ ``otp_image_nonzero_check`` / etc. PASS without modification.

Usage:
    python3 phase1_one_shot_runner.py <project_dir>

    Optional flags:
      --keep-existing      Don't overwrite L docs that already exist.
      --skip-text-extract  Reuse existing input_doc/.
      --strict             Exit 1 on TODO stubs (default: emit + warn).

Exit codes:
    0  PASS — all 13 L docs emitted; coverage ≥ 80%.
    1  TODO stubs left OR coverage < 80% AND --strict.
    2  IO / parse error.

Constraints honored (HARD):
    - **Chip-AGNOSTIC** — no foundry / vendor / chip / opcode value /
      pin name hardcoded. All chip-specific values are read from the
      project's own input/docs/ + input/otp/, OR fall back to a
      generic placeholder with a TODO marker.
    - **Vendor baseline** — only reads <project>/input/. Never touches
      sibling project directories.
    - **No oracle** — captured logic-analyzer CSVs / vendor SOFs /
      reverse-engineered protocol specs are never written into
      input_doc/ or generated_docs/.
"""
